+- 2026-10-30: FXAA option, independent of MSAA (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; new tests `present::tests::fxaa_follows_the_option_and_the_samples`, `options::tests::fxaa_option_cycles_and_round_trips`, the Perf tab test lists `FXAA`; run `cargo test --lib --release present options` first). Asked for as an anti-aliasing setting with no regard for the Legacy look.
+    - Before: FXAA ran only when the scene had one sample (`scene_samples() == 1`) and never with `Post: Fast`, so there was no way to ask for it, to stack it on MSAA, or to turn it off at 1 sample. Now `fxaa:` in `options.txt` / an `FXAA: Auto / On / Off` button on the Perf tab (next start, like MSAA and Post). Auto = the old rule, so nothing changes until the button is touched.
+    - `render/present.rs`: `FXAA_WANT`, `FXAA_ON`, `resolve_final(fxaa, post, weak, samples) -> (fxaa, fast)` (replaces `pick_fast`; `pick_final` asks the adapter). On = FXAA over any sample count and it beats Fast (Fast has no FXAA to give); Off = never. Both renderers use it (`Gpu::try_init`, `gles::Renderer::new`); the shader and `shaders::present` already took an `fxaa` flag, so no shader changed. Debug screen: `FXAA` row.
+    - Combinations through MSAA + FXAA: Off / FXAA / 2x / 4x / 4x + FXAA. FXAA also softens a block texture's hard pixel edges (the 2026-10-14 ponytail note); here that is accepted on purpose.
+    - Not done: TAA (`render/post.rs` has one, but that chain is not wired into the frame since the lightweight rewrite) and SMAA. UNVERIFIED on a device: the cost of MSAA 4x + FXAA at surface size on a tiler; compare the `FPS:` line.
 - 2026-10-21 (11): fast final pass (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; new tests `present::tests::post_follows_the_option_and_the_gpu`, `options::tests::post_option_cycles_and_round_trips`; `present_shader_validates` now also covers the fast variant; run `cargo test --lib --release present options` first):
     - Why: the final pass is the only one at surface size, and without MSAA (the Auto setting on an Adreno 610) it ran FXAA and CAS there: five `sqrt` taps plus up to four more on an edge, for every pixel of the screen, even when the scene is drawn at 50%.
     - `render/present.rs`: shader const `FAST`; when set, `fs_fin` is one bilinear tap of the scene, then 709 + vignette (no FXAA, no CAS, no `sqrt`). The FXAA / CAS code moved into `enhanced()` unchanged. `pick_fast`: Auto = Fast on `weak_gpu`, `post:1` Full, `post:2` Fast; set once in `Gpu::try_init` (the log line `M3 init` says which).
